WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.420
It's a thrilling race to save the planet on a course you can create yourself.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:27.020
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.740
I'm Mike. I'm Sam.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.380
I'm Sean. And I am Mockrider.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.180
Oh! That is Joe.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.960
You cannot pretend you're Mockrider.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.640
Yesterday, I was told several times that I am Mockrider.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.480
Pretty much at every level.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.000
I was told you are Mockrider.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:45.840
Yeah, Joe is Mockrider.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:46.840
Yeah, me. Oh, okay, yeah.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.620
Everyone else's copy says you, but Joe's copy says I am Mockrider.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:53.260
So your copy said me?

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.720
No, it's telling me that I am Mockrider, and I assumed everybody else's copy said Joe is Mockrider.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.200
Oh, okay. That's like super weird.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.840
It's like, hey, all this stuff is happening in the future.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.420
Joe is Mockrider.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:12.820
Guys, if you didn't figure it out, we're talking about Mockrider, and I know some of you were probably like really concerned because I didn't say Mockrider at the start.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.580
Usually I say the title of the game.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.200
This time I just read the back of the box.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.020
But hey, welcome to the Mockrider episode.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.380
It says it right on the title episode.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.820
Guys, Mockrider takes place in like the year 2,112.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.400
2112. Yeah, 2112.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.100
We're getting very close. Very close to that, and it's starting to look a lot similar.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.140
There's just oil drums everywhere.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:44.600
I bring up the 2112 thing real fast because I actually want to talk about our like date system and stuff because people are getting a little concerned here about like the integrity of this chronological order.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.860
And I'm just going to throw it out there and like restate this again.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.140
I think we did this like a couple episodes back and stuff.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:55.560
There is no way to know the chronological order of these NES games.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.720
Okay. And I'm sorry if that like ruins the premise of this show for some people.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.940
But like just to give you an example, like Nintendo swears that soccer came out in 1987.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.440
I found pictures of it in 1985.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.920
Fake news. You know, this is considered Mockrider is considered a launch game by Nintendo.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:27.460
But a very like well regarded electronic computer magazine actually has like an issue from 1986 where they say coming in August Mockrider, you know, like they actually like have a release date calendar.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:31.260
And I think like that holds more weight than Nintendo being like, yeah, 1985.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.820
At least we're trying. Yeah, I think we are trying.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:41.700
And I mean, just Nintendo might be getting their dates confused with the Japanese stuff, too, because this game came out in Japan and like late 84, early 85, something like that.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.300
So I just want to get that out of the way.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.540
I don't want anybody being like, you're not doing them in order.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.800
It's like we're doing them close enough.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:53.300
Okay. If we started reviewing like Flintstones two, then you could be like, something's wrong because we haven't even done Flintstones one yet.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.980
Again, Mike, just using a straw man against our audience.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.620
Like, well, who's yelling at you, Mike?

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:08.520
No one is yelling at me, but I'm glad you asked about people because James from Milwaukee wrote into the show just like you can at contact at NostalgiaCast.com.

