You know, there's, like...

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:41.480
You know, there's every...

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.480
There's all this stuff on the road.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.380
And you have to turn.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:44.920
And there's gas you have to use.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.920
And then there's also gear shifting.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:50.040
And there's just all this stuff off the bat.

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:52.140
And I was... It's just a lot to take on.

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.720
But I got over that pretty quickly.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.880
Cool. But that was my initial impression.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.700
And I'm with Sean here.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.500
Like, this game is just so...

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:03.240
So cool. Like, that's my initial impression.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.560
It's just, like... Even the music right when you start up.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:08.780
And that theme when you're driving is just, like, unreal.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:10.700
Great music. This is the first game that...

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.440
It's the first game I feel like a badass.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.300
You know? Like, what other NES game makes you feel like you actually are, like, in control of someone

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:19.340
who can, like, do some damage?

00:15:20.700 --> 00:15:22.260
Balloon fight. Right.

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:23.300
I... But not.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.640
Like, you know? It's like, the thing was that in common.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:26.920
Balloon fight does not.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:30.720
You know what? Ice Climber, it's like, those guys are just, like, random snow-mounted enemies.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:32.860
I guess the closest you could go is Kung Fu?

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.700
Yeah, but even... Oh, wait.

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:38.020
Joe's got something. I think I said in the Duck Hunt episode...

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.820
Quote, that you feel like a badass or something like that.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:43.200
Shooting innocent ducks.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:44.460
I'm sorry, I just love...

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:47.980
I'm sorry I just always bring up Duck Hunt, but I think I was talking about the clay discs.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.380
Okay. You feel like a badass. No way.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:51.880
I don't know. Somehow...

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:58.240
Don't listen to it. Somehow, like, shooting down evil forces known as quadrunners is a little more badass than

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:01.360
taking down innocent ducks that just happen to be in your way.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:02.620
Or discs of clay.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:05.980
I'm not saying it's more so, I'm just saying that's the last thing I ever said.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:09.400
Yeah, that was the first one that made you understand why Americans like to have guns.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.520
Yeah. Right, yeah. I was shoot clay discs.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:13.300
Okay, so that's initial impressions.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:17.000
One thing that Joe and I need to get out of the way, though, real fast, is that, like,

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:21.060
the gear thing is something everyone needs to learn, like, quick.

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:26.300
Because you might turn off this game before you ever start playing it if you don't learn that.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:30.020
Can I run through my first, like, three minutes in this game?

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:33.700
Yeah, doing that, can you work it into the objective a little?

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:45.020
Okay, so the objective of Mach Rider, at least the first mode, is to get through a course relatively unscathed

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:52.200
while also shooting the competitors, the quad runners.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:57.640
Yeah, not competitors. Shooting the quad runners, avoiding obstacles, and going hella fast.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:16:59.900
But here's the problem.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:05.700
When I first turned on this game, I didn't read the manual, didn't know what those numbers were at the top,

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:07.900
so I was just holding the accelerate button.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.700
I thought that was as fast as I was going to go.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:11.820
That's the problem me and Joe had, too.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:13.380
And I think this is, like, a problem everyone has.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.080
That's why you've got to read the manual.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:17.860
Thank goodness Sam the manual smith is here.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:19.780
Sam, tell us what happens with the gears.

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:21.320
You change them.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:27.180
You start in one, and then you only go so fast, but you hear your engine revving,

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:30.300
and then you press up and down in the D-pad to change gears,

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:34.680
and you press up to go, you know, to a higher gear,

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:40.340
and you can hear your car shift or your super bike shift, which is really cool,

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:43.880
especially when you're going, you downshift to do a curve or something.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:45.600
Right, yeah, yeah. And it goes, boo!

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:47.000
It's really cool.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.060
I got a nice little...

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:53.260
However, what happens to make you realize that you're playing the game wrong

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:57.280
is that there will be quad runners that come up behind you

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.320
and just run into you and you explode.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.140
Yeah, if they go faster than you and they touch you, then you die.

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:04.080
And that's what I was alluding to before,

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:07.080
where after my initial great impression, I was like, wait, this sucks.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:09.840
Because you can see them coming in the mirror,

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:12.040
but it's still almost impossible to dodge them.

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:15.080
It's, like, frightening. It's like you see them, and you're trying to, like, get out of the way,

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.720
but you just can't move fast enough.

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:21.480
And then once I realized you could shift gears, I was like, okay, this is great again.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.980
But I wish...

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:27.280
Yeah, I think reading the manual makes a world of difference,

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:30.320
because then you know off the bat that you can do that.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.680
So let's talk about the fighting course first.

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:33.920
That's the first mode.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:37.060
There's ten sectors, and it starts off really interesting

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:39.460
where it, like, shows you your path options,

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:41.900
and you choose between path A or path B.

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:45.200
It's basically spaghetti, so you can't really tell which path is which.

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:47.780
But they are two different courses.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.340
And what I found interesting, too, is, like,

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:54.000
I took, like, both of the introductory paths,

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:56.500
and there's not, like, that much difference.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.340
Like you said, since it looks like spaghetti,

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:00.540
it's just, like, the amount of turns and stuff like that.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.060
That's what you're comfortable with, I guess.

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:05.220
But there's no way of, like, you know, on your first try,

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:07.520
like, knowing, like, oh, this is the easier path.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.900
And I don't even know if that's, like, a guaranteed thing.

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:11.400
That one's easier than the other.

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:16.640
I feel like even when you're playing them, it's hard to tell what the path is doing.

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:20.020
You know, it's not like, oh, and here comes, like, the big loop thing.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.300
It just, you're just kind of taking it section by section.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:28.800
Right. And, you know, when you're in gear four, that's like, you're going so fast

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.500
that it doesn't, you know, it doesn't even matter.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:33.220
Like, you have to just kind of, when you see a turn coming,

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.380
it's hard left, hard right.

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:39.480
I think that, like, for me, the strategy during the fighting course,

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:42.420
which is, you know, again, you're just trying to get to the end of the level

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:46.860
without losing all your lives, which you cannot do in the first level,

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.980
which is nice. Like, the very first level, you can't lose all your lives.

00:19:50.480 --> 00:19:51.560
You don't have lives yet.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:53.800
You get lives in the second level.

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:55.580
And then from there, you can immediately lose.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.780
But you're just trying to get to the end of the path.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.160
And I like that objective.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:02.740
But you're also trying to, like, shoot down cars for points,

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:05.860
shoot down barrels, shoot down rocks.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:07.920
I don't even think you can blow up the rocks, though.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:09.180
No, rocks are indestructible.

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:10.800
Rocks also aren't in the first level.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:11.800
Oh, okay. That's good.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:14.700
Now that you're mentioning this,

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:16.820
I think that I went about the fight mode all wrong.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.660
Because I played a lot of endurance and solo.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:23.200
And in those, you want to go as fast as you can the whole time.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:26.080
Right. But in fight mode, you just want to finish and you want to survive.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:29.380
So I feel like I went a little bit too fast in fight mode.

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:31.000
Especially considering it's lives.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:35.520
Yeah, that's what I mean. I had assumed that fight mode was more about shooting as many things down

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:36.400
and getting the points.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:38.660
Because I deliberately didn't do that.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.600
Because I was like, I just want to see what each level is.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:43.860
So I was like, I'll just try and get through this.

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:46.480
Yeah. I would also like to note, we keep saying shooting,

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:49.780
but that's not the only way to take down the quad runners.

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:52.440
You can block them, make them run into the barrels.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:53.380
And I think that's so cool.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:56.760
I'm glad you said that because I think a bad version of this game,

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.580
especially because it's such an early NES game too.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.720
No, but a bad version of this game also would have been

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:04.860
any collision with an enemy of any kind blows you up.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:07.380
You know? Even if you get them from the side,

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:12.060
your car will be destroyed because it's just two collision objects being detected.

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:14.580
But Mog Rider took the time to be like,

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:16.920
hey, if you're on the side and you bump in hard enough,

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:19.780
they'll skid over to the right, hit the barrel, and blow up.

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:21.720
You get the points. The energy as well.

00:21:21.720 --> 00:21:22.700
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:26.080
Yeah. So I think that that aspect,

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:32.760
like that mechanic of a vehicular battle just by bumping into each other.

00:21:32.940 --> 00:21:33.860
Yeah. Yeah, road rage.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:35.500
Even like, not aspects,

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:37.080
maybe some aspects of Twisted Metal,

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:39.080
of just like bumping into each other

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:43.040
is what made me feel like a cool guy.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:44.600
Like a pretty cool guy.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:50.360
Nice. Yeah. I definitely liked bumping them into stuff more than just shooting them down.

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:53.260
But I do think like shooting them down is pretty cool.

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:54.840
I mean, let's be real.

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:57.340
Even the way you die in this game is like badass.

00:21:57.820 --> 00:21:59.440
Yeah, you just explode slowly.

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:01.100
You explode and then reanimate.

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.000
I'm fine. Yeah, whatever.

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:06.160
But then you just come back to life.

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.620
It's not like in most games you would just like pop back in,

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:11.860
but they actually took the time to reverse animate the explosion,

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:13.100
putting you back together.

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:14.960
Yeah. It's great particle effects.

00:22:15.420 --> 00:22:17.980
So just to wrap up the fighting course here,

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:21.760
every time every level gets a little harder than the ones before it.

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:25.820
The quad runners don't become any like more interesting.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:28.680
They just change colors so that like instead of one shot,

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:29.860
it's two shots, three shots.

00:22:29.980 --> 00:22:32.040
And then finally, the last one requires four shots.

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:33.160
And those are the black cars.

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:35.260
But I think that they take six.

00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:38.840
Six. Okay. I don't know where I came up with four, to be honest.

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:41.140
Maybe I was just like, hey, four.

00:22:42.400 --> 00:22:44.560
Anyway, so you go through the 10 sectors.

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:47.920
Does anybody know what happens after you get through the first 10?

00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:50.520
Can I also say, before we talk about that,

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:53.380
can I just mention too that in every beginning of every level,

00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:55.940
there's like one short sentence about what it is,

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:58.860
followed by you are mock writer.

00:22:59.160 --> 00:23:01.620
Like it was kind of funny to me because it was like,

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:05.800
I get a mock writer 10 times.

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:06.980
It's like your hype song.

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:09.900
Honestly, I want a coach to like go in and like,

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:11.500
you know, like there's always like, you know,

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:14.780
clear eyes, full hearts, can't lose from Friday Night Lights.

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:16.980
It's like, I want someone to just like, you know,

00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:18.200
give like an awesome speech.

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:19.760
And then at the end, just be like, remember kids,

00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:21.960
you are mock writer.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:23.300
And everyone just charges out like,

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:28.640
I want that to be like what I hear in the morning when I wake up.

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:31.620
I just open my eyes and then I hear you are mock writer.

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:37.160
It's actually sad that there is no like voice synthesis in this that says you are mock writer.

00:23:37.260 --> 00:23:38.380
Cause I would have appreciated that.

00:23:38.460 --> 00:23:42.200
But Mike, I don't know what happens at the end because I'm not good enough at this game.

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:43.520
Yeah, I did not make it that far.

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:45.860
So after, after you get through the first 10 sectors,

00:23:46.100 --> 00:23:48.100
you get 10 new sectors.

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:49.540
Oh, okay. No, no, no.

00:23:49.600 --> 00:23:50.780
But I think that is kind of cool.

00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:54.260
It's not just like, Hey, do these 10 again.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:56.800
You know, it's not like at the end of the 10 sectors,

00:23:56.800 --> 00:24:01.480
it's like, aha, I've kidnapped your daughter, your only daughter.

00:24:01.840 --> 00:24:04.840
But later that same day, later that same day,

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:06.340
the apocalypse is back and everything.

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:10.040
So you get 10 new sectors and then you go back to the original 10.

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:12.740
So unfortunately for mock writer enthusiasts,

00:24:12.740 --> 00:24:15.060
there is no like a wrap up.

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:18.640
There's no warm feeling inside when you finish the game of like,

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:20.740
you've stopped the apocalypse or anything.

00:24:21.340 --> 00:24:23.800
And each one has an A and a B also.

00:24:23.980 --> 00:24:25.380
Yes. That's, that's a lot.

00:24:25.380 --> 00:24:26.280
Yeah. That's a lot of courses.

00:24:26.560 --> 00:24:28.180
What happens at the end of the next 10?

00:24:28.280 --> 00:24:31.540
Do they make it? Oh yeah. You just go back to the, no, you just go back to the first 10 again.

00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:33.300
I thought there was like a very quick, like.

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:34.420
I don't know who gets that far.

00:24:34.540 --> 00:24:37.920
Yeah. I have no idea who gets to the 30, but that's pretty cool.

00:24:38.140 --> 00:24:42.860
If you do. I saw one guy had like maxed out his high score thing.

00:24:42.860 --> 00:24:43.860
So that was cool. Wow.

00:24:44.240 --> 00:24:45.660
So that's, that's fighting course.

00:24:45.820 --> 00:24:47.140
Any last thoughts on that?

00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:49.640
I did the worst on this one.

00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:50.840
Great. Yeah.

00:24:50.960 --> 00:24:51.820
Proud of you. Thanks.

00:24:53.900 --> 00:24:56.820
All right. So we're going to move right on into endurance mode.

00:24:57.000 --> 00:25:03.120
Now this one plays a little differently because instead of a finish line, there's a, you know,

00:25:03.200 --> 00:25:07.440
like a, you have to get to a certain amount of kilometers in a certain amount of time.

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:09.360
However, there's still enemies.

00:25:09.420 --> 00:25:10.600
There's still obstacles.

00:25:10.600 --> 00:25:15.660
So while the objective is speed in this one, you do have to make sure that you don't continue

00:25:15.660 --> 00:25:20.300
to get killed. Otherwise you won't be able to make it to the end in the distance that they actually do.

00:25:20.500 --> 00:25:21.900
How do people feel about endurance?

00:25:21.900 --> 00:25:29.000
I had a lot more fun in endurance because, um, I could never stay alive that long.

00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:33.620
Um, but I think that since endurance is a little bit more forgiving, like you're going

00:25:33.620 --> 00:25:34.920
to make it through a few levels.

00:25:35.180 --> 00:25:39.460
Uh, even if you blow up a few times because they give you ample time.

00:25:39.460 --> 00:25:45.940
Um, and also if, um, at the end of time you can still inch forward a bit at, at the, at,

00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:49.500
when it's a, once the time hits zero, you just can't hit the gas anymore.

00:25:49.500 --> 00:25:51.180
It just, you can still shoot stuff.

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:52.220
You can also still shoot stuff.

00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:57.580
So you slowly, and like there was one point at like the last level that I finally cleared,

00:25:57.780 --> 00:26:01.720
um, where I wasn't there yet and it hit zero.

00:26:02.180 --> 00:26:07.320
And during that, um, that slow down, I finally cracked that cam.

00:26:07.880 --> 00:26:10.900
That's cool. I didn't know that that was, uh, the way it worked.

00:26:11.020 --> 00:26:16.080
Yeah. That slow down feeling though is like, it's, it's gut wrenching a little bit when you

00:26:16.080 --> 00:26:18.820
start to just slow down and you're holding down that accelerator because you never let

00:26:18.820 --> 00:26:24.500
off of it. You know, you're like, Oh, I need to like, if anything, I will, I will ramp up to gear

00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:27.040
four, cruise through that as much as I can.

00:26:27.460 --> 00:26:32.220
And then if I see like a turn coming up or something, I'll attempt to go down to three,

00:26:32.400 --> 00:26:34.960
but I can't, you can't do one and two.

00:26:35.080 --> 00:26:36.520
Like it's, it's just not worth it.

00:26:36.620 --> 00:26:39.100
I think those are there just to, to get up to speed.

00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:42.100
Right. But not only just to get up to that speed too though, but also to like prevent someone

00:26:42.100 --> 00:26:43.920
from just going top speed so quickly.

00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:46.820
Like if there was only a two gear thing, you just go right back up.

00:26:46.920 --> 00:26:48.220
I did. I kind of wish it wrapped.

00:26:48.220 --> 00:26:52.100
I kind of wish that you could go up again to get to one from four.

00:26:53.540 --> 00:26:54.360
Okay. You know what I mean?

00:26:54.360 --> 00:26:55.260
That'd be bad for your bike.

00:26:55.900 --> 00:26:59.740
Yeah. I mean, I know that's not how, like how, but on a bike you could easily, you could like,

00:27:00.060 --> 00:27:03.800
I mean, I don't know how to ride a motorcycle, but you could, you could just switch to one.

00:27:03.900 --> 00:27:05.740
You don't have to like, you're not out of control.

00:27:06.080 --> 00:27:12.680
You switch and go, but you do, if you want to have a good time, even though you can change

00:27:12.680 --> 00:27:14.560
from like fourth back into first.

00:27:14.560 --> 00:27:18.520
Joe, just because you are the Mach Rider doesn't mean you can decide how the motorcycles work.

00:27:18.660 --> 00:27:19.520
Well, this is a super bike.

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:20.660
It's not a magic bike.

00:27:20.880 --> 00:27:22.420
It took the plunger, the whole plunger.

00:27:22.420 --> 00:27:29.140
One other quick aspect of this game that I think pertains to what we're talking about

00:27:29.140 --> 00:27:30.240
with the gears.

00:27:31.220 --> 00:27:36.560
Once you go through parts of the course, it will immediately freeze over.

00:27:36.760 --> 00:27:42.860
You just go into an ice storm and you have to be a lot more careful or you will just end

00:27:42.860 --> 00:27:44.060
up in the shoulder.

00:27:44.060 --> 00:27:46.360
I love how that slippery works too.

00:27:46.560 --> 00:27:49.080
It's a little better than the oil and stuff like that.

00:27:49.980 --> 00:27:54.840
Yeah. There's even, after you get to the, I think it's after two levels where there's a little

00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:57.800
bit of ice, there's one level that's just the entire level is ice.

00:27:57.940 --> 00:28:02.480
Really? Yeah. I think I got there on solo mode.

00:28:02.700 --> 00:28:09.260
Okay. But I just wish that there was an option to choose to go immediately into an all ice level

00:28:09.260 --> 00:28:14.660
from the beginning. Because I think that being able to practice on an all ice level would be really convenient.

00:28:14.820 --> 00:28:18.340
Because I found some things that I think help out a lot.

00:28:18.460 --> 00:28:22.400
You do need to just, when you're going into a curve on an ice level, you've got to downshift

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:24.720
and I was even letting go of the gas.

00:28:24.900 --> 00:28:30.520
And I was trying a trick that I learned from F0, which is when you go around a sharp turn,

00:28:30.660 --> 00:28:32.680
you just tap A instead of...

00:28:33.880 --> 00:28:35.580
Just to get a little bit of a throttle.

00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:38.720
Yeah, just a little bit. So I was doing that a little bit, letting go sometimes and downshifting.

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:40.240
And using your balloon fight skills too.

00:28:40.860 --> 00:28:41.820
Yeah, of course.

00:28:43.160 --> 00:28:45.400
But yeah, endurance mode was my favorite mode.

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:50.900
I'm going to speak out against the, like, being able to select ice levels though, because

00:28:50.900 --> 00:28:54.640
I just think, like, you know, in a way that's kind of like, I wish there was a way to just

00:28:54.640 --> 00:28:56.580
get to 8-4 in Super Mario Bros.

00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:58.220
so that I could practice that level.

00:28:58.300 --> 00:28:59.220
Well, they got the warp pipes. I wouldn't want them to...

00:28:59.220 --> 00:29:00.720
They got the warp zone. I know, I know.

00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:03.680
But it's like, you know, it's only four levels into it.

00:29:03.720 --> 00:29:05.640
That's fair. I just, like, wish for me that I could...

00:29:05.640 --> 00:29:08.620
No, I know, I know. Because I think that is frustrating when you get up to a certain point.

00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:10.640
I'll say this for the endurance mode.

00:29:10.820 --> 00:29:15.540
There is, like, you know, to Sean's point, it's a little forgiving at first, but I'll

00:29:15.540 --> 00:29:18.620
say that once you get to, like, 45 kilometers...

00:29:18.620 --> 00:29:19.640
Yeah, you gotta be trucking.

00:29:19.680 --> 00:29:21.240
You gotta be it. You gotta be doing pretty good.

00:29:21.380 --> 00:29:23.080
And you gotta have minimal deaths.

00:29:23.360 --> 00:29:30.140
Mm-hmm. I also found that if you spend more time in endurance mode trying to shoot things than trying to

00:29:30.140 --> 00:29:31.780
finish the course, you'll get a higher score.

00:29:32.340 --> 00:29:34.340
Like, I went through a couple times.

00:29:34.600 --> 00:29:37.720
Sometimes... Oh, yeah, because you're getting so many points just for the distance you go.

00:29:37.920 --> 00:29:43.860
Yeah. But you don't get more for, like, finishing faster or anything, or additional distance.

00:29:44.180 --> 00:29:45.920
You don't get, like, leftover time.

00:29:46.040 --> 00:29:48.040
Yeah. Right, right. I played it a couple different ways.

00:29:48.200 --> 00:29:51.800
I played it once where I was just trying to avoid everyone and get to the finish as fast

00:29:51.800 --> 00:29:54.740
as I could. And then I played one where I was trying to shoot everything.

00:29:55.340 --> 00:29:59.240
And I got, like, triple the score when I was shooting everything.

00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:07.180
We'll move away from endurance course and talk about solo course very fast because it's

00:30:07.180 --> 00:30:08.600
not much to talk about. It's the same mode.

00:30:08.900 --> 00:30:10.060
It's the same as endurance, but without any enemies.

00:30:10.240 --> 00:30:11.240
Without any enemies.

00:30:11.480 --> 00:30:13.960
But, uh, Sam, you seem to have liked this one the most.

00:30:14.120 --> 00:30:16.020
Well, not the most. I think I liked endurance the most.

00:30:16.120 --> 00:30:20.420
Oh, okay. But, uh, solo I felt was really good when I was trying to come to grips with the game.

00:30:20.740 --> 00:30:23.460
You know, when I was trying to figure out how to, how it works, really.

00:30:23.660 --> 00:30:26.380
I think you really learn from solo more than anything else.

00:30:26.380 --> 00:30:29.640
It's like, I think solo was where I felt more in control of my bike.

00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:34.000
Like, you were talking about tapping A and stuff like that and figuring out about downshifting.

00:30:34.060 --> 00:30:35.260
That's like where you learn how to drive.

00:30:35.540 --> 00:30:43.100
Yeah, exactly. That's, if only there was like a, uh, you know, a driving test for, you know.

00:30:43.660 --> 00:30:46.040
I don't know. No one actually wishes for that stuff.

00:30:46.180 --> 00:30:50.300
Like, I remember in Gran Turismo, like, four, you have to get your driver's license before

00:30:50.300 --> 00:30:52.020
you can even drive a car in that game.

00:30:52.120 --> 00:30:54.120
And it's so annoying, some of the tasks.

00:30:54.120 --> 00:30:57.260
So, thank goodness in Mach Rider, it's like, there are no laws.

00:30:57.400 --> 00:31:02.860
So, you both, like, left the modes that you were playing and then moved over to solo for

00:31:02.860 --> 00:31:04.680
a bit? I don't, I wouldn't say I left him.

00:31:04.860 --> 00:31:06.380
I think I tried each one of them.

00:31:06.500 --> 00:31:09.480
And then in solo, I was like, I'm doing pretty good in this because there's not a lot going

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:11.280
on. Yeah. So, I did that one.

00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:15.640
I think the interesting thing about that is Nintendo usually structures these early games

00:31:15.640 --> 00:31:17.380
with, like, mode A, easy.

00:31:17.740 --> 00:31:20.240
Mode B, challenging version of easy.

00:31:20.480 --> 00:31:23.060
Mode C, totally different version that's a lot harder.

00:31:23.060 --> 00:31:25.000
You know? If there is a mode C.

00:31:25.220 --> 00:31:29.840
But for me, it's like, this last mode is almost like what should have been at the top.

00:31:29.980 --> 00:31:31.560
Just like a training wheels kind of thing.

00:31:31.700 --> 00:31:34.000
But what I think is really cool is kind of like that.

00:31:34.120 --> 00:31:38.740
Like, I feel like in a lot of the games that we've been playing, A and B have been kind

00:31:38.740 --> 00:31:41.140
of similar, but ones like the hard mode, like you just said.

00:31:41.300 --> 00:31:45.780
But this, I felt like these were distinct modes, you know, with different objectives.

00:31:46.120 --> 00:31:47.280
I'd say A and B are distinct.

00:31:47.900 --> 00:31:49.140
I mean, yeah, I think that...

00:31:49.140 --> 00:31:52.440
Well, I would just say that, like, to me, that's the point I was making is, like, mode

00:31:52.440 --> 00:31:59.400
C, the solo course, is actually just, like, the game A version of mode B, the endurance

00:31:59.400 --> 00:32:00.320
course. Yeah, yeah.

00:32:00.440 --> 00:32:02.020
Right. It's almost upside down.

00:32:02.260 --> 00:32:06.380
Right, yeah. Sorry it's confusing to anyone at home, but, like, basically it's like, you know, mode A,

00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:10.060
mode B, mode C, and in this one it's mode C, mode B, mode A.

00:32:10.580 --> 00:32:15.460
But the picture that you clicked on to listen to this is probably the screen that we're

00:32:15.460 --> 00:32:17.360
talking about. Hopefully.

00:32:17.600 --> 00:32:18.720
I might make it that woman.

00:32:19.700 --> 00:32:28.300
Okay. Yeah, I mean, I basically just went from, I played all three modes to try them, and then

00:32:28.300 --> 00:32:32.000
I actually just went back to, what's the first one called, fighting?

00:32:32.180 --> 00:32:35.940
Fighting, yeah. So that's the one I played the most, so really the second and third mode I just played enough

00:32:35.940 --> 00:32:37.260
to, like, get an idea of it.

00:32:37.260 --> 00:32:40.940
But the first one was the one that I really was, like, trying to see how far can I get

00:32:40.940 --> 00:32:42.060
in this. How'd you do in the first one?

00:32:42.120 --> 00:32:43.360
Just curious. Okay.

00:32:43.680 --> 00:32:46.560
I mean, I got, I think, like, to round nine or something.

00:32:46.680 --> 00:32:48.060
I wasn't willing. Oh, wow. Hey, very nice.

00:32:48.060 --> 00:32:50.280
This was after a lot of trying.

00:32:50.680 --> 00:32:52.560
That's still pretty good, though. And I did not have a very high score.

00:32:52.740 --> 00:32:54.580
What was your tactics?

00:32:54.900 --> 00:32:58.200
Did you go fast? Did you go slow and then speed up when there were guys or something?

00:32:58.200 --> 00:33:02.680
I was going relatively slow until, like, people started coming up, which is pretty quick.

00:33:02.860 --> 00:33:06.080
Yeah. And I would go, I think, gear four as much as I could.

00:33:06.080 --> 00:33:07.560
But it's, like, fair two.

00:33:08.880 --> 00:33:10.060
It did take me a while, though.

00:33:10.100 --> 00:33:12.800
I definitely had to restart several times.

00:33:13.660 --> 00:33:18.640
But, yeah, I think it was just kind of shifting between fast and slow and, like, not worrying

00:33:18.640 --> 00:33:20.760
as much about time and just worrying about, like, being careful.

00:33:21.220 --> 00:33:26.320
Yeah. Yeah, I got to, like, round six, I think, or sector six.

00:33:26.560 --> 00:33:32.140
But I think I would have kept going in that if there was even just, like, the slightest bit of story.

00:33:32.240 --> 00:33:33.800
Because, again, like, this world is so cool.

00:33:33.800 --> 00:33:36.080
I would have loved some lore or something like that.

00:33:36.260 --> 00:33:37.520
Like, just anything.

00:33:37.680 --> 00:33:40.340
Like, on the screen, it's like you arrive out of town.

00:33:40.500 --> 00:33:41.500
Yeah, yeah, yeah. There's no one there.

00:33:41.600 --> 00:33:43.180
Exactly. Like, something super small.

00:33:43.300 --> 00:33:45.240
I don't need anything in the mode itself.

00:33:45.240 --> 00:33:47.020
Like, I didn't need a boss or anything.

00:33:47.520 --> 00:33:51.560
I just thought that, like, that would have kept me going back to the premiere mode, the

00:33:51.560 --> 00:33:55.920
fighting course. Whereas, for me, the game became more of just, like, this is really fun.

00:33:55.920 --> 00:33:59.180
I'm just working. I worked more on, like, endurance and solo than fighting.

00:33:59.340 --> 00:34:01.360
I think, like, round six for fighting and I was done.

00:34:01.540 --> 00:34:06.340
Right. One thing I would like to say, since we're kind of talking about this setting again and the

00:34:07.040 --> 00:34:13.580
story or lack thereof, I want to, I think that Nintendo was kind of self-censoring themselves

00:34:13.580 --> 00:34:18.620
because this world shouldn't, this isn't an alien invasion world.

00:34:18.880 --> 00:34:24.140
This is, like, those quad riders, those should be people.

00:34:24.520 --> 00:34:28.700
Like, I think that the fact that they've made them aliens was so that you aren't just brutally

00:34:28.700 --> 00:34:34.020
massacring these people on the road and making them something other entirely.

00:34:34.580 --> 00:34:40.740
But I think that the soul of this game requires them to be other, like, post-apocalyptic

00:34:40.740 --> 00:34:41.580
wastelanders.

00:34:41.760 --> 00:34:43.220
Okay. That's just my opinion.

00:34:43.400 --> 00:34:44.460
Yeah, that's how I played it.

00:35:22.360 --> 00:35:26.060
And so, believe it or not, there is another mode in this game.

00:35:26.060 --> 00:35:27.620
They are really packing this one in.

00:35:27.620 --> 00:35:32.700
And this one is what makes this game part of the Black Box Programmable series.

00:35:32.700 --> 00:35:34.740
This is the last one of the programmable games.

00:35:34.740 --> 00:35:39.260
If you remember, the other two were Excitebike and Wrecking Crew.

00:35:39.720 --> 00:35:43.940
We all seemed pretty jazzed about the Excitebike one enough to get us drunk on calling it an

00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:45.040
essential game at first.

00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:46.760
Thankfully, no more.

00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:51.960
And then Wrecking Crew, Joe, made some incredible levels out of that.

00:35:52.020 --> 00:35:53.180
I'm still blown away by those.

00:35:53.340 --> 00:35:56.820
They were really well done. I do like course creations, which I was excited about.

00:35:57.820 --> 00:36:00.560
Did you know going in that there would be a course creator?

00:36:00.760 --> 00:36:02.960
Or did you stumble into the title screen and just be like, oh my gosh.

00:36:03.040 --> 00:36:07.600
I knew because after, in the weeks after the Excitebike episode, when I was feeling all

00:36:07.600 --> 00:36:11.220
that guilt, I was looking up and seeing what other course creator racing games there were.

00:36:11.320 --> 00:36:13.120
And I was like, oh, there's another one, The Fouling Ear.

00:36:14.400 --> 00:36:20.640
So, Joe, since you are the level designer around here, if you will, what were your thoughts

00:36:20.640 --> 00:36:21.600
on design mode?

00:36:21.600 --> 00:36:30.120
I thought the course creation was very easy to make, very intuitive and easy to make cool,

00:36:30.240 --> 00:36:34.420
twisty, turny tracks and whatnot.

00:36:35.240 --> 00:36:39.260
And basically, just so you have a picture of it, you have two screens, sort of.

00:36:39.440 --> 00:36:41.280
And on the top screen, it is blank.

00:36:41.680 --> 00:36:45.760
And you select which tile you want to put something.

00:36:45.880 --> 00:36:49.540
And you hold B to select on the bottom screen where you have a bunch of different options

00:36:49.540 --> 00:36:51.240
of what tile to put there.

00:36:51.840 --> 00:36:52.920
So, it's pretty simple.

00:36:53.680 --> 00:36:55.200
And I was like, oh, this is really cool.

00:36:55.480 --> 00:36:57.220
Until I went to play my course.

00:36:57.400 --> 00:36:58.840
And it's kind of disappointing.

00:36:59.160 --> 00:37:00.900
Like you guys were saying earlier.

00:37:01.240 --> 00:37:03.360
You can't really tell. Yeah, you can't tell it's your course.

00:37:03.540 --> 00:37:04.380
And there are all those obstacles.

00:37:04.540 --> 00:37:06.360
While I was creating the course, I forgot about all the obstacles.

00:37:06.540 --> 00:37:07.540
You can't add them.

00:37:07.660 --> 00:37:09.780
They just randomly generate on your course.

00:37:10.040 --> 00:37:11.660
Depending on what level it is.

00:37:11.660 --> 00:37:18.220
Because that's another thing. It adds, you just keep playing it until, but in the different settings.

00:37:18.420 --> 00:37:23.840
Like you play in the desert and then you play it in the jungle or the forest or whatever that is.

00:37:23.920 --> 00:37:28.540
I think the only thing that this game, in general, needs to make it more,

00:37:28.680 --> 00:37:32.000
like the course being a bigger part of the experience,

00:37:32.200 --> 00:37:35.620
is it needs a mini-map in the corner.

00:37:35.820 --> 00:37:39.960
I think there is real estate on the screen to put that there.

00:37:39.960 --> 00:37:46.660
And I think as long as you have at least a rough approximation of the course in front of you in some way,

00:37:47.420 --> 00:37:49.960
that anticipation of like, oh, there's that hairpin turn.

00:37:50.140 --> 00:37:51.540
Like I have to get ready for that.

00:37:51.620 --> 00:37:55.420
That will affect the game for you enough to make it worthwhile.

00:37:55.740 --> 00:37:59.460
I wonder if that's like a limitation of memory for the mini-map.

00:37:59.620 --> 00:38:01.880
It probably is. I could imagine that being pretty strenuous.

00:38:01.900 --> 00:38:05.000
But I think later games might have something like that.

00:38:05.120 --> 00:38:07.260
Yeah. I do think that's a great idea though, Sean.

00:38:07.380 --> 00:38:09.660
It's something I didn't ever consider being a problem.

00:38:09.960 --> 00:38:15.280
In the game. I think just going back to something that we talked about real fast during the beginning,

00:38:15.380 --> 00:38:17.060
the design mode thing needs to be said again,

00:38:17.340 --> 00:38:19.860
is that, yeah, it's super easy to do this.

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:22.840
And I love how like you'll pick like, you know,

00:38:22.900 --> 00:38:26.000
they give you a bunch of different options for the lengths and turns of your track.

00:38:26.020 --> 00:38:29.440
And then even after you pick that length, it'll be like, hey,

00:38:29.620 --> 00:38:31.000
here are the only remaining,

00:38:31.180 --> 00:38:34.780
it'll only highlight the options that you could possibly use to continue your track.

00:38:34.780 --> 00:38:38.320
It won't let you try to make like some ridiculous thing that won't be able to be finished.

00:38:38.440 --> 00:38:40.480
It always lets you, it always tells you like, okay,

00:38:40.600 --> 00:38:42.400
you can use some of these four options now.

00:38:42.480 --> 00:38:47.540
Like that's cool. However, it's just, even though it's so easy to use,

00:38:47.620 --> 00:38:51.020
it's so unimpressive at the end of it, just because it, you know,

00:38:51.160 --> 00:38:53.800
the game, we were talking even about the speed that you go and stuff like that.

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:56.480
It doesn't feel like ownership of your own course.

00:38:56.700 --> 00:39:00.440
It just feels like a randomly generated thing when you get out there because yeah,

00:39:00.520 --> 00:39:02.020
you might remember that you were like, oh yeah,

00:39:02.080 --> 00:39:04.000
I programmed a left turn and then a hard right turn.

00:39:04.140 --> 00:39:05.420
It's like, you might remember that,

00:39:05.500 --> 00:39:08.960
but I think it's different in excite bike when you're like, oh yeah.

00:39:09.020 --> 00:39:14.340
And then I put the big hill and then there's a strip of grass and there's a booster on the left side

00:39:14.340 --> 00:39:15.380
followed by the right side.

00:39:15.460 --> 00:39:16.320
I think they really,

00:39:16.580 --> 00:39:19.220
it really could have benefited from something where it's like,

00:39:19.340 --> 00:39:22.480
I'm going to put a piece with rocks here or I'm going to,

00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:23.960
I'm going to add,

00:39:24.720 --> 00:39:30.780
I'm going to add like lots of barrels over here or this is going to be an ice section over here or something like that.

00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:32.180
That would definitely be a memory issue.

00:39:32.500 --> 00:39:33.340
Yeah, but I think like,

00:39:33.520 --> 00:39:35.520
no, I think I understand what you're saying.

00:39:35.560 --> 00:39:37.640
I think that the way I would have gone about that,

00:39:37.740 --> 00:39:44.760
and again, this is someone with no programming knowledge is like you would create the course first and then similar to like how in excite bike,

00:39:44.940 --> 00:39:47.500
you were actually like in the excite bike mode,

00:39:47.700 --> 00:39:48.740
placing your stuff.

00:39:48.920 --> 00:39:51.940
It'd be cool if you then went on the course as mock rider and,

00:39:52.480 --> 00:39:59.500
like drove forward and then like cycled with B to cycle through your things and you would place them where mock rider was.

00:39:59.600 --> 00:40:00.860
that'd be a pain to drive.

00:40:01.060 --> 00:40:02.460
That'd take forever. It would,

00:40:02.600 --> 00:40:03.420
but I mean, you're only,

00:40:03.640 --> 00:40:04.540
you know, like if you think about it,

00:40:04.600 --> 00:40:05.840
even the course of Nintendo design,

00:40:05.960 --> 00:40:08.240
it's not like they were like, and we're going to put the rock here.

00:40:08.680 --> 00:40:10.940
Some of them were though. This is exactly where people will be.

00:40:11.100 --> 00:40:12.920
There was, there was one level.

00:40:13.160 --> 00:40:13.960
I don't know if it's only,

